speechtext:
Just a moment;
I shall answer my hon. friend immediately and effectively. No parliament on earth has more experience in matters having to do with war expenditures than the parliament at Westminster, and I am prepared to say

that this government will follow with respect to war expenditures exactly the procedure followed by the parliament at Westminster. My hon. friend knows very well that the reason the parliament at Westminster has not opened the doors, put up the blinds and done the other things suggested by my hon. friend is that it regards the war as far too serious a matter .to permit a lot of unnecessary discussion to take place in the nature of political controversy.
